WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.939 line:100%,end
A refuel is logged on the phone
from the unit page.

00:00:03.939 --> 00:00:08.900 line:100%,end
Scan the unit's QR code
and tap Log a refuel.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.496 line:100%,end
The date is filled in.
Enter the litres and the meter reading.

00:00:13.496 --> 00:00:18.200 line:100%,end
A receipt photo and a note
are optional.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.467 line:100%,end
Tap Save refuel.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:24.400 line:100%,end
Only litres and readings are logged for a refuel.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:31.938 line:100%,end
The app calculates consumption between refuels:
litres per 100 km or per hour.

00:00:31.938 --> 00:00:37.500 line:100%,end
The maintenance person and the administrator see
the refuels on the unit page.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:44.045 line:100%,end
If consumption differs by more than 20 percent
from the average, the row is highlighted.

00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:50.000 line:100%,end
A sudden change can point to a fault,
so it is noticed in time.
